window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-a6a989baaa6c03f2"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"automate-bug-triage\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"bug\">自动整理 Bug 分诊</h1> <p>把日常缺陷报告整理成优先级清单，再自动运行排查流程。</p> <p>让 Codex 检查近期告警、问题、失败检查、日志和聊天报告；先在一次对话中调整清单，再按计划定期运行。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>缺陷分散在 Sentry 告警、Slack 讨论串、Linear issue、GitHub issue、失败的 PR 检查、支持工单或日志中的团队。</li> <li>希望先在一次 Codex 对话中手动运行并调整分诊流程，再安排定期运行的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果缺陷来源包括 GitHub，可读取 issue、拉取请求、评论、审查讨论串和失败的检查。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/sentry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$sentry（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果排查涉及告警，可检查生产环境错误、堆栈跟踪、受影响的发布版本和事件上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取团队成员报告缺陷的频道或讨论串，并为团队频道准备摘要草稿。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取缺陷队列、查找现有 issue、起草更新，或在分诊后准备关联的跟进任务。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Bug 上下文从哪里收集</td> <td>Sentry 告警、Slack 频道、Linear 视图、GitHub issue、PR 检查、支持队列、值班记录、日志、仪表板和部署记录</td> <td>指明 Codex 应排查的确切队列、频道、视图、代码仓库、告警链接、仪表板和文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Codex 如何读取这些内容</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a>（用于 Slack、Linear、GitHub 和 Sentry）、连接器、<a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP 服务器</a>、代码库 CLI、链接、导出文件、附件和粘贴的日志</td> <td>有现成集成时，安装并使用该集成。对于 Codex 暂时无法读取的内部来源，可构建或配置小型 MCP 服务器、CLI、导出文件或仪表板链接。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>运行一次 Bug 分诊</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请为 [repo/service/team] 进行一次 Bug 分诊，检查最近 [time window] 内的情况。\n\n使用这些插件：[@Sentry / @Slack / @Linear / @GitHub / none]\n\n输入来源：\n\n- Sentry：[project / alert link / none]\n\n- Slack：[channel / thread links / none]\n\n- Linear：[team / project / view / issue query / none]\n\n- GitHub：[repo / issue query / PR checks / none]\n\n- 其他：[logs / support tickets / deploy link / dashboard / attached file / none]\n\n输出格式：\n\n首先，列出你无法访问的输入来源。\n\n然后按 P0 到 P3 的优先级排序，返回缺陷清单。\n\n如果没有发现缺陷，请写明：没有发现符合条件的缺陷。\n\n每个缺陷都要包含：\n\n- 优先级：P0、P1、P2 或 P3\n\n- 标题\n\n- 证据（链接或简短引用）\n\n- 建议的下一步\n\n规则：\n\n- 不要发布、创建、指派、加标签、关闭、重新运行或编辑任何内容。\n\n- 将重复报告归并到同一个缺陷下。\n\n- 将观察到的证据与猜测分开。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e\">在 Linear 中使用 Codex</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用方法</h2> <p>让 Codex 检查缺陷通常出现的地方：Sentry 告警、Linear issue、GitHub issue、PR 检查、部署日志、支持工单和 Slack 讨论串。先手动排查一轮，在对话中调整报告，然后再安排定期任务。</p> <p>整个分诊流程都在同一条 Codex 对话中进行：</p> <ol> <li>按需运行一轮排查，生成缺陷清单草稿。</li> <li>检查清单，并在同一条对话中给出反馈。</li> <li>从这条对话为分诊工作安排定时任务。</li> <li>可选：如果你认可报告，可以让 Codex 起草 Linear issue、Slack 更新、GitHub 评论或交接记录。</li> </ol> <p>开始之前，先安装 Codex 需要的<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（本地尚未收录）</a>，例如 Sentry、Slack、Linear 或 GitHub。在起始提示词中，把方括号内的插件列表替换为实际的 <code>@</code> 插件标签。然后将每个方括号内的来源替换为确切的搜索位置：Sentry 项目或告警 URL、Slack 频道或讨论串、Linear 团队/视图/查询、GitHub 代码库/issue 查询/PR 检查，以及部署链接、日志文件、支持队列或仪表板。</p> <p><a id=\"phase-1-run-the-sweep\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"1\">阶段 1：运行排查</h2> <p>如果本地上下文有帮助（例如测试、代码库工具、构建检查或 CI 失败），请从负责这些缺陷的代码库启动 Codex。如果缺陷来源能通过插件、连接器、MCP 服务器、链接、导出文件、粘贴的日志或附件访问，也可以从任意代码库启动排查。</p> <p>先运行上面的起始提示词。只保留本轮排查实际需要的插件和来源。</p> <p>例如，填写完整的提示词可以写明要使用哪些插件，以及要检查哪些具体队列、频道或代码库。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">一条 Codex 提示词示例：提及 Slack、Linear 和 GitHub 插件，并列出本轮 Bug 分诊要检查的确切来源 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/bug-automation-light.png\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>一条 Codex 提示词示例：提及 Slack、Linear 和 GitHub 插件，并列出本轮 Bug 分诊要检查的确切来源 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/bug-automation-light.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"phase-2-make-the-report-useful\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"2\">阶段 2：让报告真正有用</h2> <p>在自动运行之前，先确认报告足够清晰，值得每天阅读。</p> <p>好的首轮结果应满足以下条件：</p> <ul> <li>高信号缺陷按 P0 到 P3 排序。</li> <li>重复报告归并到同一个缺陷下。</li> <li>每个缺陷都附有证据链接或简短引用。</li> <li>猜测与观察到的事实分开列出。</li> <li>每个缺陷都给出简短的建议下一步。</li> </ul> <p>安排定时任务之前，先在同一条对话中调整报告。你可以让 Codex：</p> <ul> <li>再检查一个来源，然后再给清单排序。</li> <li>忽略团队已经知道的噪声告警。</li> <li>只返回 P0 和 P1 缺陷。</li> <li>如果 Slack 报告、Sentry 告警和 GitHub 失败指向同一个问题，就将它们合并。</li> <li>为每个缺陷提供最有用的一条链接。</li> <li>补充足够的证据，让其他人能够复现问题或将其交给合适的人处理。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"phase-3-automate-it\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"3\">阶段 3：自动运行</h2> <p>按需生成的报告达到预期后，留在同一条对话中，并<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">为该分诊工作安排定时任务</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。Codex 可以使用你在对话中完善的内容来编写周期性提示词。</p> <p><strong>安排分诊任务</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task for the bug triage workflow we refined in this chat.\n\nSchedule: [every hour / every weekday morning / daily]\n\nUse the same sources, priority rules, duplicate grouping, evidence style, and P0-P3 report format from this chat.\n\nWhen you write the prompt for this scheduled work, include the plugin mentions or connected-source instructions the scheduled run needs to read those sources again.\n\nKeep the scheduled work draft-only. Do not post, create, assign, label, close, rerun, start fixes, or edit code.\n\nBefore you schedule it, show me the task prompt, schedule, sources, and action policy.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请为我们在这段聊天中完善的缺陷分流工作流安排一项定时任务。\n\n计划：[every hour / every weekday morning / daily]\n\n沿用这段聊天中的来源、优先级规则、重复项分组、证据风格，以及 P0-P3 报告格式。\n\n为这项定时工作编写提示词时，应包含定时运行再次读取这些来源所需的插件提及或已连接来源的使用说明。\n\n让定时工作只生成草稿。不要发布、创建、分配、打标签、关闭、重新运行、开始修复或编辑代码。\n\n安排之前，先向我展示任务提示词、运行计划、来源和行动策略。</div></div> <p><a id=\"phase-4-route-follow-ups\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"4\">阶段 4：分派后续工作</h2> <p>定时报告效果良好后，再决定接下来如何处理。Codex 可以为团队频道起草 Slack 更新、为需要跟踪的缺陷创建 Linear issue 草稿、为失败的 PR 起草 GitHub 评论，或为值班人员整理交接内容。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update the bug triage task scheduled from this chat.\n\nAfter each scheduled run, draft the follow-up I need:\n\n- Slack update for [channel]\n- Linear issues for [which bugs should become issues]\n- GitHub comment for [issue / PR / failing check]\n- Handoff note for [team / on-call / owner]\n\nRules:\n\n- Draft the follow-up in Codex first.\n- Do not post to Slack, create Linear issues, or comment on GitHub until I explicitly approve that action.\n- Include links to existing Linear, GitHub, Slack, or alert sources when available.\n- Keep draft-only behavior for any action not explicitly approved.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请更新这段聊天中已经安排的缺陷分流任务。\n\n每次定时运行结束后，起草我需要的后续内容：\n\n- 发往 [channel] 的 Slack 更新\n- 针对 [which bugs should become issues] 的 Linear 问题\n- 针对 [issue / PR / failing check] 的 GitHub 评论\n- 给 [team / on-call / owner] 的交接说明\n\n规则：\n\n- 先在 Codex 中起草后续内容。\n- 在我明确批准相应行动之前，不要向 Slack 发布消息、创建 Linear 问题或在 GitHub 上发表评论。\n- 存在已有的 Linear、GitHub、Slack 或告警来源时，附上对应链接。\n- 对任何未获明确批准的行动，继续只生成草稿。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"automate-bug-triage\">Automate bug triage</h1> <p>Turn daily bug reports into a prioritized list, then automate the sweep.</p> <p>Ask Codex to check recent alerts, issues, failed checks, logs, and chat reports, tune the list in one chat, then run that sweep on a schedule.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams that track bugs across Sentry alerts, Slack threads, Linear issues, GitHub issues, failing PR checks, support tickets, or logs.</li> <li>Triage workflows you want to run manually in one Codex chat before scheduling the work.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">github (online)</a></td> <td>Read issues, pull requests, comments, review threads, and failed checks when GitHub is part of your bug intake.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/sentry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$sentry (online)</a></td> <td>Inspect production errors, stack traces, affected releases, and event context when alerts are part of the sweep.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Read the channels or threads where teammates report bugs and prepare a draft summary for a team channel.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/linear\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">linear (online)</a></td> <td>Read bug queues, find existing issues, draft updates, or prepare linked follow-up tickets after the triage pass.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Where bug context gathers</td> <td>Sentry alerts, Slack channels, Linear views, GitHub issues, PR checks, support queues, on-call notes, logs, dashboards, and deploy notes</td> <td>Name the exact queues, channels, views, repos, alert links, dashboards, and files Codex should sweep.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>How Codex reads it</td> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a> for Slack, Linear, GitHub, and Sentry; connectors; <a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP servers</a>; repo CLIs; links; exports; attachments; and pasted logs</td> <td>Install the existing integration when there is one. Build or configure a small MCP server, CLI, export, or dashboard link for internal sources Codex cannot read yet.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Run a Bug Triage Sweep</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Run a bug triage sweep for [repo/service/team] covering the last [time window].\n\nUse these plugins: [@Sentry / @Slack / @Linear / @GitHub / none]\n\nInput sources:\n- Sentry: [project / alert link / none]\n- Slack: [channel / thread links / none]\n- Linear: [team / project / view / issue query / none]\n- GitHub: [repo / issue query / PR checks / none]\n- Other: [logs / support tickets / deploy link / dashboard / attached file / none]\n\nOutput format:\nFirst, name any input source you could not access.\nThen return a prioritized list of bugs, sorted from P0 to P3.\nIf you find no bugs, say: No qualifying bugs found.\n\nFor each bug, include:\n- Priority: P0, P1, P2, or P3\n- Title\n- Evidence (links or short citations)\n- Recommended next action\n\nRules:\n- Do not post, create, assign, label, close, rerun, or edit anything.\n- Group duplicate reports under one bug.\n- Keep observed evidence separate from guesses.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Codex MCP</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-434ee24ee096022e\">Use Codex in Linear</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <p>Ask Codex to check the places where bugs already appear: Sentry alerts, Linear issues, GitHub issues, PR checks, deploy logs, support tickets, and Slack threads. Start with one manual sweep, tune the report in the chat, then run it on a schedule.</p> <p>Use one Codex chat for the whole triage loop:</p> <ol> <li>Run an on-demand sweep and get a draft list.</li> <li>Review the list and give feedback in that same chat.</li> <li>Schedule a task for the triage work from that chat.</li> <li>Optional: ask Codex to draft Linear issues, Slack updates, GitHub comments, or handoff notes when you are confident in the report.</li> </ol> <p>Before you start, install the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins (not in this local snapshot)</a> Codex needs, such as Sentry, Slack, Linear, or GitHub. In the starter prompt, replace the bracketed plugin list with real <code>@</code> plugin chips. Then replace each bracketed source with the exact place to search: a Sentry project or alert URL, Slack channel or thread, Linear team, view, or query, GitHub repo, issue query, or PR check, deploy link, log file, support queue, or dashboard.</p> <h2 id=\"phase-1-run-the-sweep\">Phase 1: Run the sweep</h2> <p>Start Codex from the repo that owns the bugs when local context helps: tests, repo tooling, build checks, or CI failures. You can also run the sweep from any repo if your bug sources are available through plugins, connectors, MCP servers, links, exports, pasted logs, or attachments.</p> <p>Run the starter prompt above first. Keep only the plugins and sources that are part of your sweep.</p> <p>For example, a filled-in prompt can name the plugins and the exact queues, channels, or repos you want in the sweep.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">A Codex prompt that mentions Slack, Linear, and GitHub plugins and lists the exact sources to check for a bug triage sweep · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/bug-automation-light.png\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>A Codex prompt that mentions Slack, Linear, and GitHub plugins and lists the exact sources to check for a bug triage sweep · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/images/codex/use-cases/bug-automation-light.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h2 id=\"phase-2-make-the-report-useful\">Phase 2: Make the report useful</h2> <p>Before you automate, make sure the report is useful enough to read every day.</p> <p>A useful first run has:</p> <ul> <li>High-signal bugs sorted from P0 to P3.</li> <li>Duplicate reports are grouped under one bug.</li> <li>Each bug has linked evidence or short citations.</li> <li>Guesses are separated from observed facts.</li> <li>Each bug has a short recommended next action.</li> </ul> <p>Tune the report in the same chat before you schedule it. You can ask Codex to:</p> <ul> <li>Check one more source before ranking the list.</li> <li>Drop noisy alerts that the team already knows about.</li> <li>Only return P0 and P1 bugs.</li> <li>Merge Slack reports, Sentry alerts, and GitHub failures when they point to the same bug.</li> <li>Show the single best link for each bug.</li> <li>Add enough evidence that someone else can reproduce or route the issue.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"phase-3-automate-it\">Phase 3: Automate it</h2> <p>When the on-demand report is useful, stay in the same chat and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule a task for the triage work from it</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>. Codex can use what you refined in the chat to write the recurring prompt.</p> <p><strong>Schedule the triage work</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Schedule a task for the bug triage workflow we refined in this chat.\n\nSchedule: [every hour / every weekday morning / daily]\n\nUse the same sources, priority rules, duplicate grouping, evidence style, and P0-P3 report format from this chat.\n\nWhen you write the prompt for this scheduled work, include the plugin mentions or connected-source instructions the scheduled run needs to read those sources again.\n\nKeep the scheduled work draft-only. Do not post, create, assign, label, close, rerun, start fixes, or edit code.\n\nBefore you schedule it, show me the task prompt, schedule, sources, and action policy.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"phase-4-route-follow-ups\">Phase 4: Route follow-ups</h2> <p>Once the scheduled report is useful, decide where the work should go next. Codex can draft a Slack update for a team channel, write Linear issues for the bugs you want to track, write GitHub comments for a failing PR, or produce a handoff for whoever is on call.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update the bug triage task scheduled from this chat.\n\nAfter each scheduled run, draft the follow-up I need:\n\n- Slack update for [channel]\n- Linear issues for [which bugs should become issues]\n- GitHub comment for [issue / PR / failing check]\n- Handoff note for [team / on-call / owner]\n\nRules:\n\n- Draft the follow-up in Codex first.\n- Do not post to Slack, create Linear issues, or comment on GitHub until I explicitly approve that action.\n- Include links to existing Linear, GitHub, Slack, or alert sources when available.\n- Keep draft-only behavior for any action not explicitly approved.\n</code></pre>"};
